  "text": "sasha: quick a11y check please 12 I adjusted the compact menu in model rows so it becomes an icon-only overflow at <640px. PR: https://stash/redwood/pr/5321. worried about keyboard discoverability + SR verbosity.\ntrent: jumping in. what does the DOM look like now?\nmaya: it's an <button class=\\\"overflow-toggle\\\"> with an svg, and we removed the visible label to save space. we left title attr and no aria-label.\nnoah: title alone is unreliable for SRs. use a visible sr-only label or aria-label. for interaction semantics, native <button> is fine, but ensure aria-haspopup and aria-expanded reflect the popup state.\nsasha: good call. also the overflow menu animates with transform: translateY which hides our box-shadow focus. we should ensure focus ring persists during animation.\ntrent: prefer outline for focus so transforms don't clip it. example css: ```css .overflow-toggle:focus-visible {outline:3px solid var(--focus-600); outline-offset:2px; border-radius:6px;} ``` keep token but compute mix for dark theme.\nmaya: one more: in compact rows we collapsed some status chips into the overflow to reduce clutter. keyboard users can't discover them unless we add a menu item for status. is that OK?\nnoah: it's fine if the menu lists the collapsed items and they are semantically grouped with role=\\\"menu\\\" and aria-label=\\\"Row actions\\\". but avoid role mismatches: if it's a simple list of links, use role=list + role=listitem. menu semantics imply arrow-key interaction.\naria-qa: note: VO/JAWS treat role=menu differently. If you choose menu, implement proper keyboard handling (Arrow keys move focus, Enter activates). If you leave it as a plain popup with a list, Tab/Shift+Tab is acceptable. whichever, be explicit in docs.\nsasha: for SR copy, what should the overflow button read? currently designers like short phrasing.\ntrent: suggest aria-label=\\\"More actions for Model X\\\" or if we can generate dynamic text: \\\"More actions for \\\"Model A\\\"\\\". include model name to disambiguate when scanning rotor lists.\nmaya: implemented a tiny sr-only text too: `<span class=\\\"sr-only\\\">More actions for Model A</span>` inside the button and aria-hidden on the svg. seems robust.\nnoah: make sure the sr-only node doesn't duplicate announcements with aria-label. use one approach not both. aria-label on the button is simplest. sr-only copy is ok when you need full text for older SRs.\naria-qa: testing checklist: 1) Tab to overflow button on mac/VO -> VO announces dynamic aria-label once; 2) open menu with Enter/Space and arrow nav works if role=menu; 3) focus ring visible during animation and at 200% zoom; 4) collapsed chips exposed in menu with clear labels like \\\"Quantized: yes\\\"; 5) ensure no duplicate announcements when menu opens. I'll test today EOD.\nsasha: copy nit for menu items: prefer explicit verbs, e.g., \\\"Open model details\\\" not just \\\"Details\\\". helps when items appear in a list.\nmaya: noted. also found a contrast regression: the menu background on dark theme uses var(--panel-50) which makes the small separator lines low-contrast. I'll compute a mix to bump separators to 3:1.\ntrent: small code snippet for computed color: ```css .menu__separator {background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--panel-50) 80%, black 20%);} ``` avoid changing base tokens.\nsasha: action items: maya to add aria-labels and outline focus + compute mixes, trent to update keyboard handling docs depending on role choice, aria-qa to validate on VO/NVDA with zoom and rotor sweeps. I'll tag designers for sign-off on copy. thanks team :white_check_mark:",
